    "created_at": "2020-09-03T11:24:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-03T11:24:04Z",
    "body": "I think we should keep firing `beforeunload` if we are firing `unload` events etc without the prompt. It's consistent with other behaviors in Chrome like tab closing (see [code](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/master:content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.h;l=404;drc=2ab5162b45ef02abb590cd4fdaf7fc8a51f2dd6e)). It seems like prompting is already not required in [prompt to unload steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#prompt-to-unload-a-document) and this seems like a reasonable case for the UA not to show the prompt?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
