    "created_at": "2020-09-07T11:07:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-07T11:07:09Z",
    "body": "I don't think this matches any tracking protection mechanisms. Those rely on not fetching content. Not on rendering it and then deciding to toss it.\r\n\r\nWhat comes to mind is dealing with crashes in an event loop and how a browser might deal with those. This should probably be equivalent to that in terms of observable behavior.",
